## 28-slot roster and physical round trip

The flattening is the declared satellite-major, beam-minor rule `a = 7*l + j`. For a real compact V0.25 anchor, [`ActionRoster.from_v025_rows`](./src/modqn_bridge/bridge.py) consumes `users`, `row_user_column`, `legacy_action_index`, `identities=(NORAD, beam-chain)`, and decision-instant `visible & d2_eligible & cell_reachable`. A `legacy_action_index == -1` audit row is excluded. Duplicate legacy slots, duplicate physical identities, bad shapes/types, or a legal slot without an identity are rejected. The production provider constructs action indices and physical identities together ([provider row metadata](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:543)) and explicitly uses `-1` only for non-action audit rows ([audit row](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:653)).

