**Round-trip result:** the executable invariant is `(NORAD, beam-chain) → legacy slot → (NORAD, beam-chain)`, checked for every legal entry. It passed for 18/18 legal options across two shuffled, production-shaped TRAIN KAT rosters and for all 28 coordinate slots. This is also structural for every admitted roster because construction rejects duplicate identities and slots. To comply with the no-physics rule, no live development anchor was generated or evaluated; therefore these are development-form KATs, not a claim that the identities of a live anchor were opened in this job. Any future development-anchor test must call `verify_legal_round_trip()` and require its returned count to equal the anchor's legal-option count.

## Deterministic edge rules

| Case | Legacy adapter | V0.25 | This bridge | Agreement/disagreement |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Lowest-index tie | Invalid entries become `-inf`; NumPy `argmax` returns the lowest legacy slot ([adapter rule](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-baseline-adapter/baseline_adapter.py:720)). | Stage-C `masked_argmax` also chooses the lowest index ([V0.25 rule](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:101)). | Lowest legal legacy slot. | Agree on rule. Indices belong to different action tables unless the bridge roster is used. |
| Empty mask | Returns integer `-1` / `NO_OP_ACTION`. | Physical V0.25 representation is `None`; Stage-C variable tables instead carry an explicit legal null action. | Returns `-1`; maps physically to unserved/`None` only at the future entry point. A no-op with any legal slot is rejected. | Physical behavior agrees; representation differs. |
| Per-user invalid slot | Adapter mask prevents selection. | V0.25 validates legal physical actions. | Rejects; no remap. | Agree. |
| Joint invalidity | **No rule.** `select_actions` loops independently over users ([adapter selector](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-baseline-adapter/baseline_adapter.py:747)). | Learned Stage-C reference repair maximises summed Q1+Q2 over an ordered legal catalogue and the first maximum wins ([V0.25 repair](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/src/mcrl/stagec_v025/deployment.py:125)). | Deterministically raises `JointInvalidityError`; it neither repairs nor falls back. | Disagree/inapplicable: importing the learned Q1+Q2 repair into MODQN would define a new comparator. Owner binding required. |

The fail-closed joint rule is intentional and deterministic. It prevents a jointly invalid independent MODQN profile from reaching an evaluator while leaving the scientific repair/fallback choice unmade.

