## 1. The core open question this pilot closes

The whole multi-catfish / executor arc has one unresolved hinge:

> **Can a LEARNING-style arm reach the spread that the non-learned executor has
> already proven is both *achievable* and *reward-favoured* on the faithful env?**

What is already established (and what is not):

- **Executor proves spread is reachable + rewarded.** `global_assign_decode/`
  (SDD-05/06, a non-learned channel-surrogate global-assignment decode) lights ~7
  beams and reaches the env's spread optimum on M1; the SDD-04 fixed-policy landscape
  favours spread (calibrated ω-gap **+11.87 > 0**). The env *rewards* spread.
- **The learned baseline does NOT reach it.** On the SDD-04 7-beam faithful env, the
  trained baseline MODQN (per-user argmax over a shared Q) collapses to active=1
  (modal=1) for the converged seeds (`SUBSET_2OF3_CONVERGED_COLLAPSE`; the run as a
  whole was `NOT_CONVERGED`). Collapse is reward-**suboptimal but unreached** — a
  deploy-time execution-symmetry / homogenization failure, **not** "collapse is
  costless/optimal" (codex-corrected wording; do not regress).
- **The coordinated learned deploy-changer has NEVER run on this env.**
  `coordinated_multi_catfish/` (SDD-02) overrides `select_actions` with a learned
  coordination decoder — the only catfish-family mechanism that changes the deploy
  rule. Its sole prior probe was `NO_GO` on the **old broken** (pre-2026-06-04,
  gain-less, degenerate) env → that NO_GO **does not count** as fixed-env evidence.

The pilot puts all three side-by-side, matched, on the faithful env, and reads off a
**binary conclusion either way**:

| Outcome | Reading | Thesis framing |
| --- | --- | --- |
| coordinated **≈** executor (both spread + win a neutral evidential axis over baseline, all arms converged) | the LEARNED arm reaches the spread the env rewards | **(i)** learned win — *only if* the L2 matched verdict clears the full triad and is codex-SOUND |
| coordinated **collapses / bounded / NOT_CONVERGED** but executor spreads + shows a favourable evidential axis label vs the recorded collapsing NOT_CONVERGED B0 anchor | a non-learned decoder reaches spread (the executor — and a trivial FIXED_NEAREST rule reaches/dominates it too, per L0) | **(ii)** scoped: a bounded engineering comparator datum (executor vs recorded collapsing anchor), claim-ceilinged; catfish/coordination = honest negative-result protagonist |

Each branch is a **defined, reportable outcome** (not "inconclusive unless we train
more" — see §5, no blind episode pump). Neither branch is an effectiveness or
"publishable beats-baseline" claim **by itself**: that label is reserved for a matched
verdict that clears the full triad (§6) and is codex-SOUND. Until then both branches
are READINESS / bounded-diagnostic only.

