/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:163:| LP-2 | **Exogenous-window coverage (orbital phase).** The protocol must DECLARE which exogenous-state windows (orbital phase foremost) training and eval sample. For any EUV whose geometry evolves with simulation time: a rebuilt env REQUIRES per-episode `initial_time_s` randomization over the declared support — default = uniform over one full orbital period (`prereg.lp_2_phase_distribution`) — unless a fixed window is explicitly declared+justified (decision D1b). Check: over `prereg.lp_2_sample_episodes` episodes drawn through the ACTUAL reset path (not a synthetic re-draw), the realized initial-phase distribution matches the declared one (KS distance ≤ `prereg.lp_2_max_ks`). | Declared support + measured conformance for a rebuilt env; live env: documented PIN (reset t=0 always — FAIL-equivalent disclosure, not retroactive). | [project-defined + reason: a fixed orbital phase deletes entire event classes (satellite setting/rising) from the sampled MDP; repo doc: 03 report §4 item 8 (zenith-at-t=0 artifact)] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:196:| L1-3 | **Visibility statistics.** Per-step distribution of #visible satellites (at the spec'd min-elevation) and #reachable beams per UE over ≥3 episode-length rollouts **sampled under the declared LP-1/LP-2 protocol**. **Window-conditional caveat (Amendment A1):** the measured statistics are conditional on the episode-sampling protocol; under the live protocol (every episode pinned to the t=0 window, LP-2) the 2026-06-10 measurement P(≥2 visible)=0.0 / exactly-1-visible-always describes THAT WINDOW, not the constellation's full-period behavior (a method-consistent full-period re-instantiation of the live single-plane geometry yields 0 visible ~82 % of the time — `analysis/env-foundation-2026-06-10/d1_d7_geometry_probe.py`). Rebuilt-env L1-3 MUST be measured under the declared LP-2 phase distribution. **Proxy disclosure (B7/A2):** visibility is an elevation-only proxy; the decision-relevant servable count is measured by L1-6. | Matches the EUV spec's declared targets. For a rebuilt env: P(≥2 visible) ≥ `prereg.l1_3_min_two_visible_frac` under the declared LP-2 phase distribution (so inter-satellite handover is a live decision) and effective action-space size reported. Live-env MEASURED (2026-06-10 run, superseding the draft's memory-recorded expectation): exactly 1 visible always, 7/56 actions (0.125), P(≥2)=0.0 over 90,000 UE-steps — `03-live-env-validation-report.md` L1-3 row + `artifacts/env-validation-2026-06-10/l1-3/`. Repo-sourced anchor: adjacent-sat offset ≈ 4938 km > 1000 km reachability (codex-r2 sampled, `docs/research/catfish-faithful-route-a/11-foundation-offset-saturation-fix-matched-retrain-sdd.md:113`). | [project-defined + reason: inter-sat HO is the paper's problem type — paper Eq (4) φ2 inter-satellite cost (layout L158–169); a geometry where φ2 events are unreachable changes the problem class — "scenario defect" classification, `docs/PROJECT-STATE-AND-FAILURE-LEDGER.md` lines 67–78] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:198:| L1-6 | **Servability statistics (end-to-end; Amendment A2).** Companion to L1-3, closing its proxy gap per B7: over the SAME sampling protocol as L1-3, per-step distribution of #satellites that can actually SERVE each UE — "servable" = ≥1 beam of that satellite whose env-computed deterministic link (actual pointing rule + G_T at the actual off-axis angle + G_R − FSPL − atmospherics, fading disabled per the L2-1(a) switch; all masks applied) clears `prereg.l1_6_servable_link_floor_db` SNR. Also report the servable/visible ratio per step (the measured proxy gap). | Rebuilt env (acceptance): P(#servable ≥ `prereg.l1_6_target_servable`) ≥ `prereg.l1_6_min_frac` under the declared LP-2 phase distribution — thresholds D1-linked (reading B sets target 4). Documentation-mode: report the distribution + ratio. Live-env expectation (NOT yet executed): servable ≈ 1 (nadir-fixed pointing, servable floor ≈80.7° elevation — probe `pointing_geometry`, `analysis/env-foundation-2026-06-10/d1_d7_geometry_probe.py`). | [project-defined + reason: B7 instance — D1's decision-relevant quantity is servable count, not elevation-visibility; pointing-rule decision = 04 r2 D2a; fading-disabled link switch: `channel.py:307` region (L2-1 cite)] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:211:| L2-7 | **Noise-convention consistency.** One declared noise bandwidth convention: σ² = N₀·B_alloc where B_alloc is the bandwidth THE RATE USES (per-user share W_u), or a documented deliberate deviation. Live env: code uses N₀·B_full (`channel.py:108–114`) while rate uses W_u = B/N (`step.py:755–761`) AND the repo's canonical formula uses N₀·W_u (`system-model-formulas.md` §2.15) — three-way inconsistency to resolve. NF treatment declared (live: none ⇒ implicit NF = 0 dB; TR 38.811 handheld reference = 9 dB). | One convention declared + implemented + register-disclosed; deviation from TR 38.811 Table 4.4-1 terminal characteristics itemized. | [3GPP repo file: TR 38.811 Table 4.4-1 (UE characteristics: NF 9 dB handheld, G/T −33.6 dB/K, 0 dBi); repo doc: `system-model-refs/system-model-formulas.md` §2.15; paper: Table I σ² row + Eq (2)] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:220:| L3-3 | **Metric discriminative power.** For each panel metric (M1, M2, M3, M4, M5, qos_served_fraction): evaluate under the 4 reference policies; a metric whose value is constant across all reference policies is non-evidential and must be replaced or re-derived. Known initial state: M5_active_assignment_ratio ≡ 1.0 by construction (own assignment activates own beam — `phase02_section_6_2_row_producer.py:75–89` + `step.py:405`; documented non-evidential at `converged_baseline_ablation_eval.py:9`); `qos_served_fraction` IS discriminative (0.857–1.0 observed across SDD-11 cells). | Every retained metric separates ≥2 reference policies mechanically: \|mean_A − mean_B\| ≥ `prereg.l3_3_min_separation_rel` × pooled cross-seed std for at least one policy pair; non-evidential metrics flagged/replaced. | [repo doc: `00-…-spec.md` §8 row 4; repo artifact: `artifacts/sdd11-retrain-2026-06-09/{baseline,offsetfix}/run_metadata.json` per-seed cells + `eval/*/eval_rows.jsonl` (qos_served_fraction values); project-defined criterion + reason] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:221:| L3-4 | **Constraint enforceability.** For every declared service constraint in the EUV spec (active-beam cap, per-beam UE cap, steering limit, power caps): construct a violating input and assert the env enforces it (rejection, clipping, or assignment failure). Live env: only the per-satellite aggregate power cap exists (proportional downscale, `hobs_faithful_step.py:146–159`); active-cap/UE-cap/steering do not exist ⇒ N-A rows documenting absence. | Each declared constraint enforceable-and-enforced; absences explicitly listed (feeds gap list GAP-D). | [project-defined + reason: enforceability testing; constraint VALUE choices are rebuild-SDD decisions with their own anchors — e.g. TR 38.821 Tables 6.1.1.1-4/-6 beam-layout assumptions, repo PDF] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:224:| L3-7 | **K-feasibility — active-beam-cap structural feasibility (Amendment A1).** Applies to any EUV declaring an active-beam cap K (N-A otherwise; the live env declares none → N-A). For ≥ `prereg.l3_7_n_states` states sampled under the declared LP-1/LP-2 protocol: run the pre-registered **max-coverage feasibility planner** — multi-start greedy (`prereg.l3_7_planner_restarts` starts): select ≤K active beams per satellite + a mask-respecting assignment to maximize #UEs with env-stepped rate ≥ the QoS floor — and record the served fraction per state. Purpose: separate **decision-failure** (a learned policy fails to serve — WANTED training signal, GAP-E) from **structural starvation** (NO K-beam activation can serve the floor fraction — env defect a learner cannot escape). The planner is a CONSTRUCTIVE lower bound: a state it serves is proven feasible; a state it fails is starvation EVIDENCE (greedy may under-report feasibility — recorded as such, not as proof of infeasibility). | Acceptance-mode: planner-served fraction ≥ `prereg.l3_7_min_qos_feasible_frac` at every sampled state, OR the rebuild SDD explicitly declares scarcity-as-task-feature with its own metric semantics. Probe-mode (documentation): emit the served-fraction distribution per candidate K in `prereg.l3_7_k_candidate_set` — this data drives rebuild decision D2's K choice (K is NOT hand-picked; the candidate set itself is prereg-frozen). | [project-defined + reason: K-of-N fixed-position activation is the standard beam-hopping abstraction of the repo's own refs (QMIXBH K=3, BEAMHOP-DRL 10-of-37, BHFREQREUSE K=12 — `system-model-refs/simulator-parameter-spec.md` B7); paper Eq (5) has no capacity bound ⇒ the floor-fraction threshold is project-defined; QoS floor: `holistic_rebuild_eval.py:30`] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:233:| L4-3 | **Multi-objective tension.** Under reference policies biased per-objective (max-M1 planner vs min-handover sticky policy vs load-balance round-robin): the induced (Σr1, Σr2, Σr3) triples must show real trade-off structure (no single reference policy dominates all three). | Pairwise non-domination among ≥2 of the 3 biased policies, judged on per-seed means with relative margin `prereg.l4_3_margin_rel`, on every seed. | [paper: Table II shows the paper's own env yields trade-offs across weight rows (transcription `00-…-spec.md` ref; PDF p.2837); project-defined criterion + reason] |
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/01-env-validation-standard-sdd.md:235:| L4-5 | **Paper-scale reconciliation.** M1 aggregate under reference policies vs the paper's figure envelope (2500–4000 Mbps aggregate at 50–150 users), with a term-by-term delta ledger (gains +75 dB, satellites 8 vs 4, interference, reuse spectrum accounting). The paper's own stated budget is NOT reproducible (gain-less 2 W ⇒ SNR ≈ −56 dB, served = 0 — `failure-route-ledger.md` §G; "paper-inherited modeling defect" classification per `PROJECT-STATE-AND-FAILURE-LEDGER.md` lines 67–78): the gate therefore requires a RECONCILIATION DOCUMENT, not numeric equality. **Residual formula (Amendment A1, frozen):** with observed ratio interval [obs_min, obs_max] (EUV M1 ÷ paper-envelope endpoints) and explained-factor product Π f_i, residual = max(1.0, obs_min/Πf_i, Πf_i/obs_max) — the multiplicative distance from the explained product to the observed interval (1.0 if inside). | The delta ledger accounts for the observed scale ratio; residual (per the frozen formula) > `prereg.l4_5_max_unexplained_factor` = FAIL. |  [paper: Fig 3a–6a axes (300-dpi transcription); repo doc: `docs/failure-route-ledger.md` §G lines 123–160 + `docs/PROJECT-STATE-AND-FAILURE-LEDGER.md` lines 67–78; repo artifact: SDD-11 M1 values (`artifacts/sdd11-retrain-2026-06-09/verdict.json`)] |
