/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:86:- **Mechanism:** Reuse-3 over 7 beams gives colors {0,1,2,0,1,2,0}: color 0 = {nadir, ring-3, ring-6}. K-of-N FIXED-POSITION activation therefore picks a color composition: (i) K=3 admits monochrome {0,3,6} — all active beams co-channel on the SAME B/3 sub-band (satellite uses 166.67 of 500 MHz) with maximal intra-sat co-color (nadir co-color with ring beams only 5° = 1.5·θ_3dB away under D7, inside the main lobe) — vs chromatic {0,1,2} using full B with zero intra-sat co-color: the SAME K spans a 3× per-satellite spectrum range and opposite interference regimes; (ii) pigeonhole forces ≥1 co-color pair at K=4 and ≥2 at K=5, so increasing K adds coverage but ALSO forced self-interference — breaking the implicit monotonicity behind 'smallest K clearing the threshold wins'; (iii) L2-8's criterion 'total simultaneously-used spectrum per satellite ≤ B_total' reads K·B/3 = 1.33B/1.67B at K=4/5 under naive per-beam summation ⇒ spurious acceptance FAIL vs ≤B always under distinct-sub-band counting — the reading is unpinned; (iv) whether the L3-7 planner may exploit color-aware activation changes the K-feasibility numbers. D4b's scope is explicitly INTER-satellite only — the intra-satellite color-composition surface is owned by no decision.
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:100:- **Mechanism:** The probe samples 24 h WITH Earth rotation to marginalize the Greenwich phase; D1b draws over ONE T_orbit; the live env OMITS rotation (orbit.py:122-126; 06 ledger 'earth-rotation-frozen-ground-track' = DECLARE+JUSTIFY) and no D-row chooses the rebuilt env's Earth model. The branches diverge: (a) rotating + Uniform(0,T_orbit) sweeps only ω_E·T ≈ 25.1° of Greenwich phase — under 40° plane spacing (P=9) the per-episode draw never reaches ~37% of the geometry cell (the reset-t=0 single-window failure class one level up); (b) frozen Earth + Uniform(0,T_orbit) covers the (periodic) anomaly cycle but pins constellation-vs-target RAAN alignment as a NEW arbitrary constant — so 04's claim that D1b 'covers' the constellation-phase RANDOMIZE row is false on this branch. Direct recomputation (probe-identical math, rotation toggled, RAAN swept): 180/9/1@ε15 — 24h rotating mean 5.43 / P(≥5) 0.904; one-T_orbit rotating 5.22/0.847; frozen-Earth RAAN 0/10/20/30°: mean 5.74/5.79/5.31/5.09, P(≥5) 1.000/1.000/0.977/0.838. P(≥4)=1.000 held everywhere probed (severity therefore capped at changes-numbers, not invalidates — one hunter's invalidates claim is contradicted by this measurement), but reading-B L_w≥5 feasibility, L1-3/L1-6 statistics, eval variance, and L4-4 shares all move with the undeclared choice. Separately T_orbit is double-sourced: D1b's ~6.0e3 s (Kepler at a=7151, 6018 s) vs the live paper-backed v=7.4 km/s convention (6072 s, and Fig 6b sweeps speed 7.2-7.6 ⇒ T per arm); LP-2's KS check (≤0.05) cannot catch the ambiguity (KS distance 0.0089), so the conformance gate is checking an undefined target.
