/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:125:### [F19] D5's load-dependent noise leaves every PRE-ASSIGNMENT noise consumer unpinned: candidate-link W_u is undefined (empty beam ⇒ N=0), the channel-quality snapshot/mask/planner become assignment-coupled through a second channel, L1-6's 'servable' floor has no value until a load exists (and shifts +3.57 dB vs the B_full convention — D1's sizing claim inherits an undeclared convention), the L2-2 calibration gate needs a pinned reference load + two new ledger terms + an FRF-aware comparator rule, and the L5-1 encoder bound is breachable at high per-beam SINR
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:128:- **Mechanism:** Live noise is a load-independent constant (N₀·B_full), so per-beam channel_quality, the action mask, greedy, and the L4-0/L4-2 snapshot-replay planner are well-defined per state. Under D5, σ² = N₀·(B/3)/N_{l,v} depends on CURRENT load: (a) candidate links to an EMPTY beam have N=0 (divide-by-zero or an undeclared prospective N=1 convention); whether the evaluating user counts itself is undefined ⇒ the state input and every 'fixed channel-quality snapshot' become assignment-coupled through the NOISE term, degrading planner exactness (L4-0); (b) L1-6 (Amendment A2) is a PRE-assignment gate — its SNR is undefined without a pinned reference bandwidth, and the same physical link reads +10log10(3)−1.2 = +3.57 dB higher under (B/3 + NF) than under B_full, so the meaning of the 0.0 dB floor — and the measured servable count certifying D1's 'servable-by-construction' sizing — silently depends on which convention the executor picks (the visible-vs-servable class again); (c) L2-2's 'EUV CNR' has no unique value (varies 10log10(N_b), up to ~+17 dB) — needs a pinned reference (natural: N=1, B_noise=B/3 ⇒ 17.69 dB), the 0.079 dB-residual ledger gains ΔNF = −1.2 dB and a noise-bandwidth term 10log10(166.67/400) = −3.80 dB, and the comparator-selection rule (lexicographic |Δalt|,|Δfreq|) has no FRF criterion although D4 makes FRF an EUV property tied to per-beam bandwidth in TR 38.821 Table 6.1.3.2-1; (d) the encoder maps channel_quality via log1p(snr_linear); D5 raises SINR by 10log10(3N) dB and log1p exceeds the prereg bound 10 once SINR > 43.4 dB — reached at N≈100-150 users/beam (paper sweep max 150) before Rician peaks.
