/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:139:### [F21] The acceptance-mode L4-5 paper-scale factor ledger must be re-derived from scratch: the package dissolves f1 (duty-cycle, ≥4 sats restore the paper's precondition) and invalidates f4 (measured at mean_active_sats=1.0), inverts f2's cancellation logic, introduces a new f_K = 4K/28, and in aggregate roughly CANCELS D4's ÷3 (4K·(B/3)/(7·B) = 0.57-0.95 of live total rate-bandwidth) — while the SDD's L4-5 term list still names the dissolved '8 vs 4' factor
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:142:- **Mechanism:** Live L4-5 PASS rests on f1=1.675 (8-vs-4 coverage duty-cycle, measured with mean_visible 1.20 and ONE serving sat) × f2=1.0 ('×3 over-count cancels in live/figure') × f4=0.577 (interference uplift at mean_active_sats=1.0, intra-sat only). Under the package: (i) reading-B D1+D2a restores the paper's implicit ≥4-precondition ⇒ f1 dissolves to ≈1.0 (D6 itself says the 8-vs-4 framing dissolves but draws no L4-5 consequence; the SDD ledger template still names 'satellites 8 vs 4'); a NEW factor appears: active beams = 4 sats × K vs the paper's 28-beam catalog ⇒ f_K = 4K/28 ∈ [0.43,0.71]; (ii) f2's cancellation inverts — rebuilt B/3 vs paper full-B means f2 ≈ 1/3, modulated by the D5 SINR correction (×1.06-2.05); (iii) f4 is invalid under 4-5 overlapping clusters whose cross-sat co-color hits are a D4b coin-flip, and D5's noise drop enlarges the interference-off uplift; (iv) D2a adds a low-elevation term absent live (FSPL +3.3 dB at ε15 vs 30°, beam-edge −3 dB). Net total rate-bandwidth vs live = 4K/21 = 0.571/0.762/0.952 at K=3/4/5 — at K=5 the package's aggregate M1 effect is ≈neutral, contradicting any single-decision scale expectation; with ~6 stacked ×1.5-×3 factors, the l4_5_max_unexplained_factor=2.0 verdict can flip on one mis-derived term.
