/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:155:- **Mechanism:** Inter-satellite interference IS computed and single-sourced from beam_directions_eci, which encodes nadir-fixed pointing — D2a's retarget flows through automatically ONLY IF the rebuild keeps that single seam. Two paths do NOT follow: (a) the antenna_gain_in_channel=False fallback feeds interference with per-SATELLITE gain and no pattern (every co-color beam at full gain — meaningless once multiple area-tracking satellites overlap); (b) nearest_beam mask eligibility, initial assignment, and state-encoding offsets derive from the same nadir frame. Neither is named in D2a's consequences. Separately, the interference function runs PER USER with Python loops over L·K plus an L·K-wide vector op per beam: L·K goes 56→1260 under D1 (hunter's ×506 quadratic scaling REFUTED at verification — measured ×10 step-total), plus U×L = 18,000 per-step visibility calls — contradicting 04's cheap-cost justification for 'constellation size has almost no training-cost consequence'.
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:164:- **Mechanism:** Three stacked defects. (1) D5 noise shift: L2-4's metric SNR−SINR = 10log10(1+I/σ²) was measured at σ²=N₀·B_full (median 9.95 dB, inside band); under D5 σ² shrinks by 3N_b/10^0.12 at fixed interference power (interference = full co-color beam powers, untouched by D5) ⇒ the SAME physics reads 20.1-24.6 dB at rebuilt loads — above the 15 dB bound whose stated purpose is to flag broken accounting; a correctly built env mechanically FAILs acceptance. 04 re-measures L2-4 only under D4b (:218-219); the D5-driven +10-15 dB shift is undeclared. (2) Geometry: D2a co-points all window clusters; same-pattern coloring makes every satellite's center beam co-channel; each interferer arrives within ~±8 dB of the serving signal ⇒ spread loads give median 22-25 dB degradation (simulated, both colorings) while greedy concentration on the best sat gives 0.1 dB at K=3 — BELOW the 0.5 dB floor. L2-4 requires ≥3 load patterns but states one median-band criterion with no aggregation rule ⇒ the verdict is determined by an undeclared protocol choice. (3) The other live-measured profile anchors (RR/collapse rate ordering 1.58-1.67 for L4-1; L4-2 coupling median 1.146 dB) were generated through the old noise floor and shift under D4+D5 (spread/collapse rate gap compresses ~5.7×→~4.1×). The l2_4_* prereg keys carry no D4b/D2a/D5 link tags unlike the D1/D2-linked keys.
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:171:- **Mechanism:** (1) Vacuity: breaching 1 Mbps at W_u=(B/3)/N requires N > 166.67·log2(1+SINR) users on ONE beam — at the paper-pinned 100 users total (sweep max 150) that needs SINR < −2.9 dB, while D5 raises typical SINR ~12-13 dB; even total collapse of 100 users onto one beam yields 3.3 Mbps > floor. Direct simulation on the recommended geometry: greedy/concentrated assignments serve 100% at 5.9-46 Mbps for every K∈{3,5,7} and both colorings (worst probed corner: forced spread under option (ii), 11% below floor — a pattern the max-coverage planner won't choose). So congestion can never trip the floor; L3-7's served fraction is a pure COVERAGE statistic of the K-active union geometry, every K clears 0.95, 'smallest K clearing the threshold wins' returns K=3 by construction — the 'K is NOT hand-picked' claim degenerates to the QMIXBH anchor, and GAP-E's 'service failure must be possible and visible' closes only as a geometry event, never congestion (reproducing GAP-D's warning). (2) Prereg hole: 01-SDD §4 rule 4 ('a gate whose verdict depends on a number not in the prereg is invalid by construction') — Appendix A has l3_7_n_states/min_qos_feasible_frac/planner_restarts/k_candidate_set but NO qos-floor key; the floor exists only as a hardcoded constant (holistic_rebuild_eval.py:30, 1.0e6) with a never-read yaml twin (REP-04q), and the 06 ledger classifies 'qos-floor-value' CONFIG-EXPOSE — the K-deciding number becomes user-tunable with no data-blind freeze. (3) Probe basis: 04 says L3-7 probes K 'on the D1+D2a geometry' — geometry only; served fractions are computed from env-stepped RATES, which depend on D4 (B/3), D5 (noise), D4b (regime; rate factor spans ÷1.46-÷2.83), and the ε15 edge users (+3.3 dB FSPL, −3 dB beam edge) who decide whether 0.95 clears.
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:192:- **Mechanism:** Every probe candidate hardcodes F=1, i=53°. The recommendation's load-bearing number is a floor with zero margin (P(≥4)=1.000, 5th percentile exactly 4, P(=4)=0.096 at ε15). Inter-plane phasing F controls adjacent-plane anomaly alignment and coverage-gap synchronization — the min-visible floor is the F-sensitive statistic even where the mean is not. i=53° over the 40N area yields ~1.63× density vs a uniform shell (uniform-shell E[visible] = 180·(1−cos 0.2726)/2 = 3.32 vs probed 5.43) — the sizing rides the resonance and a different i changes the whole candidate table. The floor is additionally certified only on the 24-h sampling filament (~9 crossings of the 9574-s Greenwich symmetry cell) and a 5×3 grid (50×45 km spacing) while reading B promises ≥4 for EVERY UE position in the continuous area.
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:206:- **Mechanism:** D1's consequences claim rise/set events enter the MDP and D1b calls the hovering-snapshot abstraction 'unsustainable' — true ACROSS episodes (initial-condition diversity) but in-episode the rates are small: mean pass ≈412 s ⇒ P(any set in 10 s) ≈ 12%, P(a specific window satellite sets) ≈ 2.4%, further suppressed because nearest-4 selects AGAINST about-to-set low-elevation satellites; within one episode the constellation sweeps only ~0.6° anomaly. Measured on 180/9/1@ε15 (24 h, 1-s grid, 8639 episodes): P(≥1 bound top-4 sat drops below ε_min within 10 s) = 0.0013 — quantified justification for D1c's stable-binding mitigation, currently asserted without numbers; nearest-4 IDENTITY churn over 10 s = 15.1% — harmless under per-episode redraw but load-bearing if any protocol chains windows. Gate L1-6 measures per-step servability only, not 'all bound slots remain servable through the episode' (the instantaneous-proxy class B7/A2 was written to kill). The same rate machinery (rank-4/5 crossing) is the missing input to D1c's remap-risk codex review, and episode-length-10s is never surfaced as the paper pin that bounds D1b's in-episode usefulness.
/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:213:- **Mechanism:** (a) If nearest-L_w is evaluated per user, the same slot maps to DIFFERENT physical satellites across users in one step — beam_loads, reuse-color interference sets, and the r3 reachable union all require one global beam identity. The natural choice (one area-global window, canonical slot order) is never stated in 04. (b) Even with a global window, REP-012 visibility is per-user: elevation to a given satellite varies ~1.5° per 100 km of ground offset near the floor, so a window satellite at 16-17° for the area center is below 15° for far-side users — their 7 slot-actions are masked. Measured proxy: the 4th-bound satellite starts below 17.78° in 15.1% of episodes ⇒ per-user catalog shrinkage is routine. The package should declare which referent the paper-dimension claim means and whether ε_min/visibility is evaluated at user or area-center level.
