/home/sat/route-c-wt/docs/research/env-foundation/07-design-coupling-findings.md:248:- **Mechanism:** Channel gains (hence all interference contributions) are computed only for satellites with elevation ≥ min_elevation_deg; raising ε_min to 15° (D7) silently zeroes interference from 0-15° satellites. Today that is harmless because activation is assignment-driven (D2b) and the single-area abstraction means no out-of-area co-channel traffic exists — but a 12°-elevation satellite with active area-pointed beams (FSPL only (2076/780)² ≈ 8.5 dB below zenith) would be silently non-interfering under either future change. L2-4 materiality on the rebuilt env is therefore conditional on the undeclared statement 'interferers = active beams serving THIS area, sampled through the serving visibility mask'.
